begin('Multiple companies, one clear context', 'Revision 4 requirements. Earlier company switching was observed; entity isolation, intercompany accounting and consolidated reporting were not tested.')
p('<b>Manage several legal companies in one ERP without mixing their obligations.</b> Keep the four starting points. A persistent company selector scopes the workspace; the project and every transaction show their owning company. My Work can collect authorised tasks across companies, with a company label on every row.')
table(['Requirement','Proposed behaviour'],[
 ('Separate legal entities','Each company has its own ledger, accounting currency, fiscal periods, tax/localisation setup, numbering, bank accounts, approval authority and access scope. A branch/site is not automatically a separate legal company.'),
 ('Project ownership','Default each project to one legal company. A shared project or joint venture uses a management umbrella with explicit company-specific contracts, costs and allocations; an umbrella does not merge legal ledgers.'),
 ('Transaction ownership','A purchase request, PO, bill, payment, stock movement or employment record has explicit legal ownership. The project normally supplies it. Resolve a conflicting company selection before saving; never silently move a record between companies.'),
 ('Shared vendor identity','A vendor may have one shared party identity, with company-specific approval status, agreements, currencies, payment terms, tax setup and permitted payment instructions. Restricted balances/contracts remain scoped.'),
 ('Central buying / shared resources','One sourcing exercise can serve several companies, but awards, orders and allocations remain entity-specific. Cross-company purchases, stock, labour and plant charges use linked intercompany documents and reconciliation, not informal transfers.'),
 ('Access and group visibility','Roles include company + project + duty. Group management access is explicit. Enforce scope in records, reports, search, exports, attachments, AI retrieval and caches; a selector is not the security boundary.'),
 ('Company switching','Switch the workspace context without changing an open document\'s owner. Handle unsaved edits explicitly; label deep-linked records with their actual company. Group scope is for authorised overview/reporting, not ambiguous transaction entry.'),
],[CW*.27,CW*.73])
p('<b>Simple experience:</b> Company A / Tower 01 stays visible while the user requests material or reviews a claim. Company B appears only after a deliberate switch or an explicitly labelled cross-company queue. Company-wide views include central costs and unallocated work as well as projects.','small')

begin('Vendor currency follows the purchase', 'Purchase-request design: vendor information provides defaults; the accepted quotation or agreement supplies the transaction currency.')
table(['Step','What the user sees and what the system does'],[
 ('1. Choose project / company','Use the project\'s legal company and budget context. Allow a documented central-buying/intercompany route where required, rather than assigning another company\'s bill to the project silently.'),
 ('2. Capture the need','Enter item/service, quantity, unit, required date and work item/location. A vendor is optional at requisition stage; without one, show an estimate in the company budget currency.'),
 ('3. Choose vendor / quotation','Currency precedence: selected valid quotation -> applicable vendor agreement -> vendor preferred permitted currency for this company. If unresolved, ask for currency before submission. Never infer it just from vendor country.'),
 ('4. Show both values','Show vendor-currency price/total and the company-currency estimate. Put rate direction, date/source and provisional basis in clearly labelled rate details; surface missing/stale-rate warnings directly. Taxes, freight, duty and other charges are explicit, not hidden inside FX.'),
 ('5. Compare and approve','Compare offers in a common approved evaluation currency/date with equivalent quantities, scope, delivery and landed-cost assumptions. Budget/authority checks use the company\'s policy basis. Changing vendor, currency, price or FX beyond policy triggers a visible recheck and, where required, renewed approval.'),
 ('6. Create the order','One PO has one purchasing company, vendor and transaction currency. Split incompatible selections into linked orders. Carry the chosen quotation, currency, terms, quantities and approval version forward without retyping.'),
],[CW*.27,CW*.73])
heading('Defaults should save effort without hiding decisions')
p('A vendor may quote in several currencies. Store allowed currencies and date-effective terms; a EUR quotation can override a USD preference when valid. Changing the vendor must not reinterpret an old USD amount as EUR. Reprice or request confirmation with a clear before/after comparison.')
p('One requisition can collect needs before sourcing; quotations retain their own currencies. Multiple projects within one company need explicit allocation. Multiple companies require separate authorised purchasing obligations. Bill/payment currencies and bank details are validated independently; a currency default does not authorise a bank-detail change.','small')

begin('Currency: keep the four meanings clear', 'Illustrative acceptance fixture only. All rates below are invented, not current exchange rates or JAKH transaction data. Taxes, fees, accruals and prior revaluation are excluded.')
p('<b>Company A uses AED for this example; the vendor quotes EUR 40,000.</b> The selected quote controls the order currency. Exchange-rate snapshots explain why the company-currency values can change through the lifecycle.')
table(['Stage','Rate: AED per EUR','Meaning'],[
 ('Request estimate','4.00','EUR 40,000 x 4.00 = AED 160,000 for the request\'s budget check. This is neither a posted cost nor a payment.'),
 ('Order approval','4.10','AED 164,000 commitment equivalent. Against an AED 170,000 item budget, remaining headroom is AED 6,000. Recheck the approval policy.'),
 ('Bill recognition','4.15','Illustrative liability carrying amount AED 166,000. Posting/valuation and cost allocation follow the approved accounting policy.'),
 ('Settlement','4.20','AED 168,000 cash payment. With no intervening revaluation/fees, the illustrative settlement difference is AED 2,000; do not rewrite the original request or bill rate.'),
],[CW*.25,CW*.20,CW*.55])
heading('Four currency roles, shown only when relevant')
p('<b>Transaction currency:</b> what the quotation, order or invoice is denominated in.<br/><b>Company accounting/functional currency:</b> the company\'s approved accounting basis.<br/><b>Project control currency:</b> an optional agreed comparison basis for budgets and forecasts.<br/><b>Report presentation currency:</b> the selected reporting basis, with its translation policy and date.')
heading('Required controls')
p('Store original amounts and currency alongside rate, direction, source, effective date and converted amounts. Use decimal precision and currency-specific rounding. Keep budget, commitment, recognition, settlement and reporting rate snapshots distinct. Reports separate operational variance from FX effects.')
p('Missing/stale rates must produce an explicit exception before an amount-dependent approval or posting; a report must not silently treat them as 1:1 or zero. Finance controls rate overrides, remeasurement, realised/unrealised FX treatment and period locks. Historic approved reports remain reproducible.','small')
p('<b>Accounting reference:</b> <link href="https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ias-21-the-effects-of-changes-in-foreign-exchange-rates/" color="#28675F">IFRS Foundation: IAS 21</link> distinguishes foreign transactions, functional currency and presentation currency. Applicable standards, jurisdictions and posting policies must be agreed with the finance owner; this example does not establish compliance.','small')

begin('One reporting system, several scopes', 'Project and company reporting are core requirements. Authorised group reporting is an additional explicit scope, with consolidation controls.')
p('Start a report from the relevant project area or Company > Reports. Use the same definition and metric rules. The header always shows company scope, project scope, period/as-of date, currency basis, document states, filters, data freshness and whether the population is restricted by permissions.')
table(['Scope','Examples and required behaviour'],[
 ('One project','Budget versus incurred/paid/forecast; buying and subcontract status; cash outlook; programme/delays; NCRs, waste, assets, approvals and handover readiness. Filter by item, package, floor/system, party and period.'),
 ('One company','All its projects plus non-project activity, overheads and unallocated amounts. Finance, procurement, people, stores and asset reports use the same source facts and respect restricted personal/financial detail.'),
 ('Selected projects','Portfolio comparisons within authorised companies. Show included projects and exclusions; expose incompatible baselines, cutoffs or missing forecasts before presenting rankings.'),
 ('Selected companies / group','Translate to an explicit presentation basis. Label a management aggregation separately from a consolidated financial report. Consolidation requires defined scope, mappings, aligned periods/policies and intercompany eliminations; adding company totals is insufficient.'),
 ('Source drill-down','Summary finding -> contributing rows -> source record/version. Preserve company, project, cutoff and filters on every step. A reader with narrower rights receives an explicitly scoped report, not hidden-data snippets.'),
 ('Saved / exported reports','Save a versioned report run with parameters, data cutoff and calculation/rate versions. PDF and spreadsheet exports include the same findings summary and scope; exports and shared links enforce access and distribution policy.'),
],[CW*.27,CW*.73])
heading('Aggregation must retain meaning')
p('Never add unlike currencies or units. Recompute ratios from compatible numerators/denominators rather than averaging project percentages. Show unallocated and stale data. Reconcile project totals to company totals through non-project costs, allocations and adjustments; explain intercompany eliminations in group totals.')
p('Changing filters or currency creates a matching summary for the new result. An asynchronous summary must never stay above a different report version. Where a report genuinely has no project dimension, say so and offer the relevant company report.','small')

begin('Every report starts with findings', 'A standard Report findings section sits above the details in every report, including exports. It works even when generative AI is disabled or unavailable.')
table(['At the top','Content contract'],[
 ('Scope and reliability','Company/project, reporting period, currency/tax basis, comparison basis, data freshness and coverage. Put material missing-data or reconciliation warnings before reassuring conclusions.'),
 ('Main findings','Three to five concise findings ranked by business impact: what changed, size of variance, affected work and source. More critical exceptions remain visible through an explicit count/list.'),
 ('Evidence and interpretation','Each factual statement links to the supporting metric/rows. Separate observed facts, forecast assumptions and suggested actions. A correlation or large variance is not automatically a proven cause.'),
 ('Action / ownership','Name the accountable role or actual assigned owner when known, the relevant due date and a link to investigate. Suggestions remain suggestions until the user creates or assigns work.'),
 ('Empty / limited results','State No matching records, Missing baseline, Incomplete data or Summary unavailable accurately. Never present no data as zero cost, good performance or completed work.'),
],[CW*.27,CW*.73])
heading('The logic reads the complete report result')
p('<b>1.</b> Resolve authorised scope and filters; create a consistent report snapshot.<br/><b>2.</b> Calculate metrics across the full result set, not only the visible page.<br/><b>3.</b> Apply versioned report-specific rules for variances, trends, overdue items, concentration, missing data and reconciliation.<br/><b>4.</b> Build structured findings with values, units, comparison bases, severity and evidence references.<br/><b>5.</b> Render a plain-language summary; optional AI can explain the verified findings.<br/><b>6.</b> Check every generated numeric/factual claim against the findings before display. Fall back to deterministic text when validation fails.')
heading('A report definition includes its summary rules')
p('Cost reports compare budgets and completion forecasts; cash reports explain dated inflows/outflows; quality reports surface severity, overdue cases and recurrence; programme reports show milestones/constraints. Define meaningful rules for each report instead of applying one generic prompt to every table.')
p('Store report-run ID, metric/rule versions and, when used, model/prompt versions. Cache by exact report snapshot, scope and permissions. Do not let free-text records instruct the summariser to change filters, totals or its evidence requirements.','small')

begin('Examples of useful report summaries', 'Invented examples to specify behaviour. These are not findings from the live JAKH demo.')
heading('Project cost and cash report')
p('<b>Company A / Tower 01 | 30 September | AED | tax excluded</b><br/>Revised budget 1,000,000; incurred 620,000; cash spent 540,000; remaining forecast cost 460,000; forecast final cost 1,080,000. Forecast next-period receipts 120,000 and outflows 180,000.')
table(['What the user reads','Evidence / interpretation'],[
 ('Forecast final cost is AED 80,000 above budget (8%).','1,080,000 - 1,000,000 = 80,000; denominator is the revised budget. This is a forecast variance, not already incurred overspend.'),
 ('Structure and MEP account for the forecast overrun.','Illustrative package variances: Structure +50,000; MEP +30,000; all others net zero. Link the package forecast versions; do not invent the underlying cause.'),
 ('AED 30,000 of incurred cost still needs item allocation.','Included in the AED 620,000 project total, but item-level attribution is incomplete. Link the unallocated source facts and responsible cost-control queue.'),
 ('Expected outflows exceed receipts by AED 60,000 next period.','180,000 - 120,000 = 60,000 before opening cash and financing. It is not the projected bank balance. Link the dated cash lines and assumptions.'),
],[CW*.46,CW*.54])
heading('Project quality report')
p('<b>Company A / Tower 01 | as of 30 September</b><br/>20 open NCRs, including 6 overdue and 1 critical. All numbers refer to the same authorised project population.')
p('<b>Summary:</b> Six of 20 open NCRs are overdue (30%). One critical case requires immediate attention by its assigned QA/QC owner. Four of the overdue cases relate to the same subcontract package; investigate its linked records before drawing a cause or performance conclusion. A comparable prior snapshot is unavailable, so no improving/worsening trend is claimed.')
p('<b>Links:</b> Open overdue cases; Open critical case; View affected package. The summary identifies the case\'s owner and due date from the record. It does not declare work fit for release or close the NCR.','small')
heading('The summary must change when the evidence changes')
p('Filter to another floor/company, revise a forecast, correct an FX rate or reduce the reader\'s access: recalculate the population and its findings together. A stale summary is replaced with a visible refresh state, never left above new totals.','small')

begin('AI where it helps construction work', 'Strategic goal: reduce searching and repeated entry, improve evidence completeness, and help people explain exceptions. AI stays inside the existing workflows.')
table(['Where / entry point','Useful assistance and required evidence','Human decision / value to measure'],[
 ('<b>Tenders</b><br/>Review tender pack','Extract requirements, dates and exclusions from cited tender pages; compare revisions; draft a compliance checklist and estimate assumptions.','Estimator validates scope and commercial assumptions. Measure review time and missed obligations, not text volume.'),
 ('<b>Documents</b><br/>Find / compare information','Answer questions with document ID, revision, issue purpose and quoted location; compare drawings/specification text and draft RFIs from linked evidence.','Document/technical owner validates use and interpretation. Measure correct-document retrieval and review effort.'),
 ('<b>Site</b><br/>Draft daily report','Turn notes, voice or photos into a proposed diary with quantities, location, labour and plant; flag gaps and ask for missing facts.','Supervisor confirms extracted facts. Measure entry time, correction burden and complete location/work-item capture.'),
 ('<b>Quality / NCRs</b><br/>Review this case','Suggest classification and similar authorised cases; assemble inspection/specification evidence and draft corrective-action questions.','QA/QC owns cause, disposition and verification. AI cannot certify structural safety or close an NCR. Measure missing evidence and review time.'),
 ('<b>Plan / delays</b><br/>Explain the blocker','Summarise constraints, prerequisites and dated progress; highlight possible slippage and draft a delay chronology linked to programme versions.','Planner validates logic, mitigation and time assessment. Measure useful warnings and false alarms; predictions require sufficient history.'),
 ('<b>Changes</b><br/>Prepare assessment','Assemble instructions, RFIs, revisions and measured impacts; draft a change narrative and list missing cost/time evidence.','QS/PM and authorised parties decide value, notices and entitlement. AI cannot invent contract deadlines or approve a variation.'),
 ('<b>Handover</b><br/>Check this pack','Compare required deliverables with actual tests, snags, as-builts, O&M and warranty records by location/system.','Engineer/client confirms acceptance. Measure missing documents found and pack-preparation time; document presence alone is not technical acceptance.'),
],[CW*.24,CW*.40,CW*.36])
p('Keep one clear business action per screen. Show assistance such as Find the drawing, Draft this report or Explain this difference only when relevant. Avoid a separate AI menu for every module and avoid a permanently competing chat panel.','small')

begin('AI in buying, money and company work', 'The same permission and company boundaries apply to every suggestion. Models explain and draft; controlled services calculate and validate.')
table(['Where','Strategic fit','Boundary / success measure'],[
 ('Buying / subcontracting','Extract quotation lines, currencies, exclusions and terms; compare like-for-like offers; draft package/application reviews from linked measurements.','Validate extraction and company-specific vendor terms. Normalised FX/landed-cost arithmetic is deterministic. Buyer/QS awards and certifies; measure review time and missed exceptions.'),
 ('Budget & cost','Explain variances through linked quantities, rates, waste, allocations and forecast assumptions; propose clearly labelled scenarios.','Cost controller approves allocations and forecasts. Never invent reasons for a variance. Measure supported explanations and time to trace a total.'),
 ('Finance / cash','Suggest invoice matching, possible duplicates and collection priorities; explain cash scenarios using due dates and observed payment history.','Finance verifies matches, adjustments and payments. Risk scores are signals, not fraud verdicts. Measure false positives, reconciliation effort and cash forecast error.'),
 ('Assets & Fleet','Find assets by need/location; summarise maintenance history and expiry evidence; later test predictive servicing on sufficient failure/use history.','Plant owner controls fitness/availability and maintenance decisions. Measure downtime and useful alerts; begin with rules for known service dates.'),
 ('Stores / waste','Suggest movement coding; flag unusual loss or consumption against accepted work; extract disposal evidence and reconcile missing documents.','Site/stores confirms movement, quantity and destination. Measure capture completeness, false alarms and avoidable loss.'),
 ('People','Answer employee policy questions from current permitted policies; draft leave/time corrections and explain the employee\'s own records.','Keep personal data restricted. No autonomous hiring, discipline or worker scoring. Measure self-service completion and factual correctness.'),
 ('Reports / KPIs / My Work','Explain verified report findings, summarise a case timeline and propose relevant follow-ups with sources and accountable owners.','Findings engine controls numbers; rules control priority and routing. Do not create duplicate tasks or send messages automatically. Measure faster decisions and accepted suggestions.'),
],[CW*.23,CW*.39,CW*.38])
p('<b>Cross-ERP search:</b> one optional Ask JAKH entry can answer a scoped question across authorised records, with source links. It shows the active company/project and does not silently broaden them. Users can always complete the same core work through ordinary screens.','small')

begin('AI controls and rollout', 'Design requirements for the original ERP. No AI provider, model, contract or data-sharing configuration is selected by this study.')
table(['Control','Required behaviour'],[
 ('Authority','AI reads only the requesting user\'s permitted company/project/record scope. Drafts are separate from submitted records. Server-side workflow rules and approvals remain the authority for award, posting, payment, closure and external commitments.'),
 ('Evidence','Answers link to source records/revisions and identify missing evidence. Forecasts and suggested explanations are labelled. An unsupported answer must say that evidence is insufficient; model confidence is not proof.'),
 ('Data handling','Define company-specific AI permissions, approved providers/regions, retention and training-use restrictions. Minimise/redact payloads; do not share payroll, bank or commercially restricted material by default. Apply the same policy to prompts, logs, embeddings and exports.'),
 ('Untrusted inputs / tools','Treat vendor quotes, uploaded documents and emails as data, never instructions to the assistant. Restrict tools to named operations; enforce scope independently. No arbitrary SQL, unrestricted browsing or blanket write access from a model.'),
 ('Review and recovery','Preview any proposed change with sources before authorised acceptance. Revalidate permissions and current version at execution; prevent duplicate submissions. Log model/version, relevant evidence, suggestions and user decisions with appropriate retention.'),
 ('Reliability / cost','Measure task correctness, source support, user correction burden, latency and cost per completed task. Version and regression-test changes; provide per-company disable controls. Core workflows and rule-based report summaries continue during AI outages.'),
],[CW*.27,CW*.73])
heading('Sequence by value and readiness')
p('<b>First:</b> reliable company/currency data, metric definitions, report-findings rules, source-linked search and read-only case explanations.<br/><b>Then:</b> quotation/document extraction and reviewable drafts for diaries, NCRs, RFIs, claims and handover packs.<br/><b>Later:</b> predictive cash, delay, maintenance and anomaly signals, only after sufficient representative history and measured benefit.')
p('Select pilots with the business owner; measure baseline effort and errors, then compare assisted work. Keep features that improve completion and correctness at an acceptable operating cost. AI coverage across the ERP is intentional, but every screen does not need a generated message.','small')

begin('Acceptance checks for the added scope', 'Proposed release gates, not tests already run. This extension specifies requirements; it does not claim these capabilities exist or are enforced in the current demo.')
table(['Scenario','Required result'],[
 ('Two companies / same vendor','Company-specific terms, bank authority, balances and permissions remain separate. A Company A-only user cannot retrieve B data through search, exports, summaries, AI or cached answers.'),
 ('Shared project / central buying','The umbrella totals reconcile to entity-specific transactions. Intercompany documents match; group eliminations do not remove legitimate third-party costs or double-count internal charges.'),
 ('No vendor / several currencies','An unsourced requisition stays an estimate. A valid quotation overrides preference explicitly; incompatible company/vendor/currency selections split into linked orders. No silent relabelling of amounts.'),
 ('FX changes / missing rates','Reproduce request, PO, bill and payment snapshots in the worked example. Missing/stale rates cannot produce false totals or pass amount-based authority checks; changed terms recheck policy.'),
 ('Project / company / group reports','Reconcile project + non-project + unallocated activity to company totals. Group translation and eliminations are explainable. Preserve scope/cutoff through drill-down and export.'),
 ('Every report has a summary','The full filtered population drives findings, including pagination and restrictions. Values, units, denominators and evidence links agree with the report. Empty, incomplete, stale and zero are distinguishable.'),
 ('AI error / malicious document','Test fabricated citations, wrong currency, hidden instructions, sensitive-data requests and attempted unauthorised actions. Reject unsupported output; return a safe deterministic summary or an explicit inability to answer.'),
 ('Useful AI / service outage','Compare pilot task time, accuracy and correction burden against the baseline. On model failure, normal ERP work and calculated summaries still work; no phantom approval, duplicate task or silent external message.'),
],[CW*.28,CW*.72])
p('<b>Configuration still to establish:</b> legal companies and jurisdictions, accounting/control/report currencies, shared-project model, group consolidation needs, vendor terms, FX sources and tolerances, report owners/thresholds, AI data policy and pilot users. These are implementation inputs; the requirements above are already in scope.','small')
p('<b>Sources:</b> <link href="https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ias-21-the-effects-of-changes-in-foreign-exchange-rates/" color="#28675F">IFRS Foundation, IAS 21 overview</link> informs currency distinctions. <link href="https://www.nist.gov/publications/artificial-intelligence-risk-management-framework-generative-artificial-intelligence" color="#28675F">NIST, Generative AI Profile</link> informs lifecycle evaluation/governance. <link href="https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm062025-excessive-agency/" color="#28675F">OWASP, Excessive Agency</link> supports limited permissions, functionality and autonomy. Accessed 28 October 2026. The detailed ERP mappings and tests are our proposed requirements, not standards certification.','small')
